p.src:
A spatial derivative makes the coupling between neighboring degrees of freedom explicit. On a lattice of spacing $\epsilon$, $\partial_x\phi(x,t)
  =\lim_{\epsilon\to0}
   \frac{\phi(x+\epsilon,t)-\phi(x,t)}{\epsilon}.$ It depends on two nearby coordinates, but it contains no generalized velocity. In the mechanical analogy it belongs to the coordinate dependence of the Lagrangian, not to the $\dot q_i$ dependence.

