p.src:
The free Maxwell Lagrangian density is $\mathcal L_{\mathrm{EM}}
 =-\frac14F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu}
 =\frac12\left(\mathbf E^2-\mathbf B^2\right).$ In temporal gauge, $\mathcal L_{\mathrm{EM}}
 =\frac12\dot{\mathbf A}^{\,2}
  -\frac12(\boldsymbol{\nabla}\times\mathbf A)^2.$ It has precisely the scalar-field pattern: squares of time derivatives minus squares of spatial derivatives.

