p.src:
The Hamiltonian shortcut is now justified: reverse the sign of the non-time-derivative term. The electromagnetic energy density is $T^{00}_{\mathrm{EM}}
 =\mathcal H_{\mathrm{EM}}
 =\frac12\left(\mathbf E^2+\mathbf B^2\right),$ and $H_{\mathrm{EM}}
 =\int d^3x\,
\frac12\left(\mathbf E^2+\mathbf B^2\right).$ Unlike the Lagrangian density, the energy density is nonnegative.

